.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-measure 1  "rev-stealth-measure " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-measure \- v1.1.0 (P15): local fingerprint diagnostics for monitoring. External SaaS calls are opt\-in via `\-\-enable\-external`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth measure\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] <\fB\-\-url\fR> [\fB\-\-enable\-external\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-egress\-probe\fR] [\fB\-\-user\-agent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Local fingerprint diagnostics for monitoring (P15). Validates the target \-\-url and emits a deterministic fingerprint snapshot. External SaaS probes (CreepJS / bot.sannysoft) require \-\-enable\-external. The VPS egress probe requires \-\-enable\-egress\-probe AND the `vps\-egress\-probe` Cargo feature.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
URL to measure against. The page is not actually fetched unless `\-\-enable\-external` is set; we only validate the URL shape here
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-external\fR
Opt\-in to external fingerprint SaaS calls (CreepJS, bot.sannysoft.com, etc.). Default: disabled
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-egress\-probe\fR
P10.5: Opt\-in to a VPS egress probe (HEAD request against a minimal endpoint) to measure exit IP / TLS / DNS leak after deploy. Even with this flag set, the probe is only active when the binary was built with the `vps\-egress\-probe` Cargo feature; otherwise a deterministic `disabled` stub is returned. Default: disabled
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-agent\fR \fI<USER_AGENT>\fR
Optional override for the User\-Agent we attribute the measurement to. When omitted we use a neutral rev\-stealth placeholder
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth measure \-\-url https://example.com
  $ rev\-stealth measure \-\-url https://x.test \-\-enable\-external
  $ rev\-stealth measure \-\-url https://x.test \-\-enable\-egress\-probe

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Measurement emitted.
  1  UserError        Bad args.
  2  TransientError   External probe transient failure (when \-\-enable\-external).
  3  PermanentError   Bad \-\-url / measurement path unavailable.

ENV:
  REV_STEALTH_EGRESS_PROBE_URL  Override the egress probe endpoint.
